If not all equal, we can have a = b ≠ c, then from (a - b) factor zero, okay. Then from (b - c) factor: b ≠ c => then 2 - λ - μa = 0. Similarly from (a - c): a ≠ c => 2 - λ - μb = 0. Since a=b, both give same condition: 2 - λ - μa = 0. So λ = 2 - μa.

Now plug into equation (1) (or (2)): 2a + λ(b + c) + μ bc = 0. Since a=b, b=a. So:

2a + λ(a + c) + μ a c = 0.

Replace λ: 2a + (2 - μa)(a + c) + μ a c = 0.

Expand: 2a + (2 - μa)a + (2 - μa)c + μ a c = 0.

Compute (2 - μa)a = 2a - μa^2. So:

2a + 2a - μa^2 + (2 - μa)c + μ a c = 0 => 4a - μa^2 
