In impartial combinatorial game with moves removing 1 or 4 tokens, the positions are determined by Grundy numbers or simply winning/losing positions: a position is losing (P-position) if all moves lead to winning positions for opponent; winning (N-position) if there exists a move to a losing position.

We need to count n <= 2024 such that starting with n tokens and Alice to move, Bob can guarantee a win. That means the starting position is a losing position for the first player (Alice). So we need to count the number of n <= 2024 that are P-positions.

