The probability that all four of Jen’s numbers match the drawn numbers is  

\[
P(\text{all 4 match})=\frac{1}{\binom{10}{4}}=\frac{1}{210}.
\]

The probability that at least two of her numbers match the drawn numbers is found using the hypergeometric distribution.  

\[
P(X\ge 2)=\sum_{k=2}^{4}\frac{\binom{4}{k}\binom{6}{4-k}}{\binom{10}{4}}
= \frac{90+24+1}{210}= \frac{115}{210}= \frac{23}{42}.
\]

The conditional probability that she wins the grand prize given that she won a prize is  

\[
P(\text{all 4} \mid X\ge 2)=\frac{P(\text{all 4})}{P(X\ge 2)}=
\frac{1/210}{23/42}= \frac{1}{115}.
\]

Thus \(m=1\) and \(n=115\), so  

\[
m+n = 1+115 = 116.
\]

\[
\boxed{116}
\]

