The user gave a transformation rule: The original query string was split on spaces, each substring's symbols reversed, then concatenated back with the separators in the same positions. So the transformed input is base64-encoded. We need to decode base64 and reverse the transformation (i.e., reverse each word again). Then print the reconstructed text using repr().

We need to output Python code that does this.

