Thus for each b, we can iterate over s such that s^2 has two digits in base b: i.e., b <= s^2 < b^2 (since two-digit numbers in base b range from b (i.e., 10_b) to b^2 - 1 (i.e., (b-1)(b-1)_b). Actually the smallest two-digit number is b (i.e., 10_b) which is value b. The largest is (b-1)*b + (b-1) = b^2 - 1. So s^2 must be in [b, b^2 - 1].

