Thus we need X = 9, Y = 9, Z = 9? But note that X is multiplied by 100, Y by 10, Z by 1. So if X=9, Y=9, Z=9, then 100*9 + 10*9 + 9 = 999. Indeed that works.

But are there other possibilities? Since X can be up to 18, but if X > 9, then 100X would exceed 900, but we could offset with negative Y or Z? No, Y and Z are non-negative, so 100X must be <= 999. So X can be 0 to 9. Similarly, given X, we have 10Y + Z = 999 - 100X.

