\[
S=50-8\sqrt6+\frac{721+200\sqrt6}{529}
   =\frac{27171-4032\sqrt6}{529}\approx32.69.
\]

Since \(\dfrac{657}{16}=41.0625\) is larger, the maximum of \(a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2}\) occurs at \((2,2,\tfrac{23}{4})\).

Thus

\[
r^{2}=\frac{S_{\max}}{4}= \frac{\frac{657}{16}}{4}= \frac{657}{64}.
\]

The fraction \(\frac{657}{64}\) is already in lowest terms (\(\gcd(657,64)=1\)).  

Therefore \(p=657,\;q=64\) and

\[
p+q=657+64=721.
\]

