Definition: n is b-beautiful if:

- n expressed in base b has exactly two digits: i.e., b <= n <= b^2 - 1 (since two-digit numbers in base b range from b (10_b) to b^2 - 1 ((b-1)(b-1)_b)). Actually the smallest two-digit number is b (represented as 10), largest is (b-1)*(b) + (b-1) = b^2 - 1.

