6a+2b+3c &\equiv 6.
\end{aligned}
\]

Solving this linear system modulo 7 yields the unique residue solution  

\[
a\equiv5,\qquad b\equiv6,\qquad c\equiv2,\qquad d\equiv4\pmod7.
\]

Since each digit must be between 0 and 9, the only possible values are  

\[
