We have an octagon with vertices independently colored red or blue with probability 1/2 each. We ask: what's the probability that there exists a rotation (by some multiple of 45 degrees) such that after rotating, all blue vertices land on positions that were originally red. Equivalent: there exists a shift k (0 ≤ k ≤ 7) such that for all i, if vertex i is blue originally, then vertex i+k (mod 8) is red originally. So B ∩ (B+k) = ∅.

