S_uv = sinθ
S_vw = sinφ
S_uw = sin(θ+φ)

All positive if convex shape with orientation.

Thus cross(u,v) = L^2 S_uv.
cross(v,w) = L^2 S_vw.
cross(u,w) = L^2 S_uw.

Now compute t, t', etc.

t = -1 + cross(w,v)/cross(u,w). cross(w,v) = -cross(v,w) = -L^2 S_vw. cross(u,w) = L^2 S_uw.

Thus t = -1 + (-L^2 S_vw) / (L^2 S_uw) = -1 - S_vw / S_uw.

t' = -cross(w,v)/cross(u,v) = -(-L^2 S_vw) / (L^2 S_uv) = S_vw / S_uv.

Thus t - t' = (-1 - S_vw/S_uw) - (S_vw/S_uv) = -1 - S_vw(1/S_uw + 1/S_uv).

Thus PR length = L * |t - t'| = L * (1 + S_vw(1/S_uw + 1/S_uv)), since negative sign but absolute.

So PR = L * (1 + S_vw (1/S_uw + 1/S_uv) ).

Now compute PQ.

We can compute Q using expression Q = w + r v. r = 1 - a where a = cross(u,w)/cross(v,w) = S_uw / S_vw.

Thus r = 1 - S_uw/S_vw = (S_vw - S_uw)/S_vw.

