Thus the centers lie on a line parallel to AC at distance r. The number of circles N that can fit is floor( (width at height r) / (2r) ) + 1, but if it's exact we have (N-1)*2r = width at height r.

We derived width at height r: w(r) = b - r*(cot A + cot C). Using data:

